    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d08d19fedb018d6b803df13899&id=8a78879ea0f4259701a116801b6d28db": {
      "title": "Office Coordinator-ARC and Counseling Services",
      "description": "Position: Office Coordinator-ARC and Counseling Services Location: Waverly, IA Job Id: 618 # of Openings: 1 WARTBURG COLLEGE Title of Position: Office Coordinator – Academic Resource Center (ARC) and Counseling Services. This is a full-time, 10-month position. Function of Position : Responsible to the Academic Success Programs Director for providing general office support for the Academic Resource Center and Counseling Services, proctoring exams for Testing Services, and supervising student workers. Duties and Responsibilities: General Office Duties – 40% Provide support for ARC and Counseling professional staff by monitoring overall office functions, maintaining office records, overseeing office equipment and supply orders, and managing scheduling and calendars as needed. Provide front line triage support for walk in visitors and concerns when student staff are not available. Respond to requests and disseminate information that requires explanation and interpretation of college and departmental policies and procedures. Perform other related duties as assigned. Academic Resource Center – 30% Serve as primary test proctor in conjunction with Disability and Access Coordinator; receive exam requests, schedule exams and exam rooms, administer exams, uphold testing policies and procedures. Supervise ARC Peers (student employees), including mentoring student manager position(s); responsible for hiring, training, scheduling, evaluation, and general supervision. Create and maintain ARC services data collection and organization utilizing Excel and other software. Counseling Services – 30% Establish and maintain department records and data collection databases utilizing Excel and other software. Coordinate the departmental budgeting process, including managing payment for bills and other expenses. Supervise Counseling student employees; responsible for hiring, training, scheduling, evaluation, and general supervision. Supervision: Definite objectives are set up for the employee by the supervisor, requiring the use of a wide range of procedures. The employee plans and arranges their own work and consults with the supervisor on unusual cases. Minimum Qualifications: Requires equivalent of two years post-secondary education; proficiency in MS Office computer applications and general secretarial skills, plus 18 months of related experience. Excellent communication, interpersonal, and customer service skills; ability to multi-task. Prefer prior experiences in an academic setting and supervisory experience. Application Procedure Please upload the following by selecting the “Apply for this Position” below: resume a letter of interest including a statement regarding qualities within the context of the Wartburg College mission contact information for three references Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d08d19fedb018d6b803df13899&id=8a78859e9d4aea68019d92b785761666": {
      "title": "Student Account Specialist",
      "description": "Position: Student Account Specialist Location: Waverly, IA Job Id: 576 # of Openings: 1 WARTBURG COLLEGE Title of Position – Student Account Specialist Function of Position: Responsible to the Director of Student Accounts for the preparation of and processing of student account information including charges, receipts, in-house student loans, monthly statements, collections, due diligence, and auditing of reports. This is a full-time, twelve-month position. Principal Duties and Responsibilities: Access administrative systems for the Business Office and Financial Aid Office to assist students, families, faculty, and staff with the following (35%): explain account information research and resolve account questions process receipts and transactions accurately and timely assist with monthly payment plan questions, cancellations, and rebalances Responsible for the following related to student accounts (35%): coordinate and generate charges/adjustments with other departments (such as Residential Life, Dining Services, Financial Aid, Registrar Office, and faculty/staff) assess monthly finance charges prepare monthly statements for current and prior students Coordinate and execute collections and due diligence on in-house loans, tuition accounts, and other accounts. (10%) Negotiate repayment terms for loans, collection accounts, and past due student accounts. (7%) Serve as the primary back-up for the Student Account Assistant. (5%) Process mail and receipts for payments on student accounts. (2%) Assist with the annual audit. (2%) Participate in on-going process improvements and document processes related to job duties (2%). Perform other related duties as assigned. (2%) Supervision: Employee is expected to proactively communicate and collaborate with Business Office and Financial Aid staff and other campus partners. Employee is expected to demonstrate initiative and pursue completion of all objectives, planning and prioritizing their own work and resolving unusual cases in consultation with their supervisor. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in business/accounting or 4 years of equivalent experience. Requires knowledge of Microsoft Office environment; strong Excel skills; accounting knowledge and strong commitment to customer service. Application Procedure: Please upload the following by selecting the “Apply for this Position” below: 1) resume 2) a letter of interest including a statement regarding qualities within the context of the Wartburg College mission 3) contact information for three references See www.wartburg.edu for further information about the college and the city of Waverly.  Screening begins immediately and continues until position is filled. Wartburg College Founded in 1852, Wartburg College is a selective four-year liberal arts college of the Lutheran Church (ELCA), nationally recognized for community engagement. The college offers more than 50 academic majors and pre-professional and certificate programs leading to the bachelor’s degree. The college is located in Waverly, Iowa, a growing community of more than 10,000 residents. As part of the Cedar Valley metro area (near Waterloo and Cedar Falls), Waverly has an abundance of cultural, musical, and recreational opportunities. Major Midwest metropolitan areas within driving distance include Des Moines, Iowa (2.5 hours); Minneapolis/St. Paul, Minn. (3 hours); Madison, Wis. (3.5 hours); Rochester, Minn. (2 hours); Chicago (5 hours); and Omaha, Neb. (4 hours). Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d08d19fedb018d6b803df13899&id=8a7883ac9e6b0bdf019e938aa72a31c3": {
      "title": "Cleaning Staff",
      "description": "Position: Cleaning Staff Location: Waverly, IA Job Id: 600 # of Openings: 1 WARTBURG COLLEGE Title of Position: CLEANING STAFF-Full-Time Function of Position: Responsible to the Director of Maintenance and Cleaning for cleaning rooms, floor surfaces, restrooms, entries, hallways, common areas, laundry rooms and kitchenettes or other designated areas.   The principal duties are especially relevant to the academic year.   Work may be performed in multiple assigned buildings. Summer responsibilities will involve work (annual cleaning) in a variety of campus buildings and assistance with preparing for and cleaning up after camps, conventions and events.  Incumbents may work with students, team members, college employees and guests of the college, treating all with respect. Principal Duties and Responsibilities: Clean according to the defined O&M standards.    Assigned core areas could be in residence halls, academic or administrative buildings, or other college owned buildings. Utilize authorized cleaning products and notify the O&M Office Coordinator when supplies are needed. Clean drinking fountains, water plants, and address other unique needs. Effectively utilize the work order system and respond to assigned tasks in a timely manner. Provide input to the work order system for needed repairs Assist in cleaning of areas other than assigned core area when needed. In collaboration with the cleaning supervisor, provide training and supervision to assigned students.  Utilizing the procedures outlined for student employees, assist in creating a positive work experience for student employees. In addition to cleaning, summer responsibilities may include transporting linen and making beds; assisting with moving furniture within weight restrictions. Work collaboratively with general maintenance staff on assigned tasks. Assist with performing event setups and teardowns as needed. Fill in for snow removal as needed. Perform other duties as assigned. Supervision: The employee proceeds alone on routine work following pre-established standard practices. Questions are referred to the supervisor.  Work schedules and priorities are primarily determined by the supervisor. Minimum Qualifications: Basic oral, written and math skills. Relevant experience preferred. Ability to lift up to 25 pounds. Ability to work with arms above shoulder height. This position will need to be flexible but normal hours are 1:00pm to 9:30pm Monday through Friday. This position will currently be on call, along with the other cleaning staff, for approximately 4 weekends a school year.  There will be special events that will require additional time which may include nights and weekends. Application Procedure Please upload the following by selecting the “Apply for this Position” below: resume a letter of interest including a statement regarding qualities within the context of the Wartburg College mission contact information for three references Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d08d19fedb018d6b803df13899&id=8a78859fa064222601a08d110c0460e5": {
      "title": "General Maintenance Staff",
      "description": "Position: General Maintenance Staff Location: Waverly, IA Job Id: 617 # of Openings: 1 WARTBURG COLLEGE Title of Position - General Maintenance Staff-Full-Time Function of Position: Responsible to the Director–General Maintenance and Cleaning for performing general maintenance work to include carpentry, electrical, plumbing, snow removal and other cleaning/repairs . Incumbents may work with students, team members, college employees and guests of the college, treating all with respect.  Work may be performed in multiple assigned buildings. Principal Duties and Responsibilities: Perform basic plumbing work. Although not inclusive, this includes repair of flush valves, traps, faucets, etc. Perform basic electrical work. Although not inclusive, this includes changing outlets, switches, lights, ballasts, etc. Perform basic carpentry work. Although not inclusive, this includes repair of furniture, replacing floor tiles, minor wall repair, etc. Monitor and perform basic repairs of building climate controls for boilers, fan coils, HVAC units, hot water heaters, chillers, pumps, air compressors, etc. If applicable, operate, repair and maintain building specific equipment (e.g. variable voltage power units, gas valves, lab top benches, ice machines, dining equipment, etc.) Repair washers, dryers, screens, blinds, vacuum cleaners, windows, and dining equipment. Perform daily inspections of building spaces and equipment, including key stakeholders, where appropriate. Check fire alarm, emergency lights and fire panels. Investigate and report roof leaks. Maintain exterior areas, including snow/ice removal and trash/recycling collection. Assist with floor care, event setups/teardowns, and occasional cleaning duties. Use the work order system to complete tasks efficiently. Collaborate with maintenance staff, dining staff, contractors, and student employees, providing constructive training when assigned. Perform other duties as needed to support campus operations. Supervision Definite objectives are set up for the employee by the supervisor, requiring the use of a wide range of standard procedures.   Work schedules and priorities are planned with input from the supervisor. Minimum Qualifications Basic oral, written and math skills Ability to read diagrams, gauges, other basic instruments, and schematics One year or more prior appliance repair experience preferred Willingness to attend both on-site and off-site training Knowledge equivalent to 1-3 years applied trades training Ability to lift up to 50 pounds Ability to work with arms above shoulder height Application Procedure: Please upload the following by selecting the “Apply for this Position” below: 1) resume 2) a letter of interest including a statement regarding qualities within the context of the Wartburg College mission 3) contact information for three references See www.wartburg.edu for further information about the college and the city of Waverly. Screening begins immediately and continues until position is filled. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d08d19fedb018d6b803df13899&id=8a7885ac9f8b9423019faa0a39932ca1": {
      "title": "Cook",
      "description": "Position: Cook Location: Waverly, IA Job Id: 610 # of Openings: 1 WARTBURG COLLEGE Title of Position - Cook-Full-Time The cook is responsible to supervisors and management staff for preparing food in the kitchen and in front of customers, recording food use data, cleaning equipment and work areas, and working with student staff. Cooks work as a team to accomplish their tasks. Principal Duties and Responsibilities: Prepare food for board plan dining, special diets, catering, and retail areas, utilizing information from rotating menus, service records, distribution summaries, recipes, sales order, and as verbally instructed by supervisors. Use proper temperature measurement and tasting methods to maintain quality standards, and seek direction or assistance if recipe adjustment is needed. (55%) Set up, operate, use, disassemble, clean and sanitize food service equipment and work areas. Wash and sanitize pans and other dishes. (15%) Accurately complete service records recording all items used, record run out times, gather recipe yields, recommend recipe improvements, help develop new recipes, and insure food quality. (8%) Cook in front of guests, plate food, serve, engage with guests and colleagues, and provide quality customer service. (9%) Ensure sanitary food production, storage and handling techniques. Label and date, and package food to be sold or issued, and unused ingredients and food items. Monitor food quality and assist with proper FIFO (first in first out) inventory usage. Check and record refrigeration temperatures. (5%) Welcome, orient, train, and supervise student employees. (4%) Receive and put away food. Compost and recycle. Sweep and mop floors. (4%) Perform other related duties as assigned. Supervision: Definite objectives are set up for the employee by the supervisor, requiring the use of a wide range of procedures. Supervisors and managers are available to answer questions, but employee must be able to work on own once trained. Minimum Qualifications: Requires 9 months effective experience, basic math, use of a calculator and scale, ability to read and follow both written and verbal directions, communication and good customer service skills, ability to lift 50 lbs. and to work effectively with students, faculty and staff. Working with others in a collaborative manner is an essential function of this position. Physical Abilities: Position requires standing, kneeling and moving except when on break. Lifting up to 50 lbs., pinching, hand/wrist position and endurance are moderate requirements of the position.  Good vision is needed to read recipes and prepare food. It can get hot when working with some equipment, and there is need to go into refrigerators and freezers. It can get noisy in the work environment due to equipment, ventilation fans, garbage disposals, and other people working in same area; work pace is determined by business activity level, equipment used and deadlines. Application Procedure: Please upload the following by selecting the “Apply for this Position” below: 1) resume 2) a letter of interest including a statement regarding qualities within the context of the Wartburg College mission 3) contact information for three references See www.wartburg.edu for further information about the college and the city of Waverly. Screening begins immediately and continues until position is filled. Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d08d19fedb018d6b803df13899&id=8a78879ea0f4259701a11bc160ff1c1b": {
      "title": "Executive Director of Advancement",
      "description": "Position: Executive Director of Advancement Location: Waverly, IA Job Id: 619 # of Openings: 1 WARTBURG COLLEGE Title of Position – Executive Director of Advancement Position Summary The Executive Director of Advancement serves as the senior operational and strategic leader within the Office of Institutional Advancement and is responsible for coordinating and aligning the work of multiple advancement functions, including annual giving, alumni and parent engagement, prospect management and research, advancement services, and donor relations. Reporting directly to the Vice President for Institutional Advancement, the Executive Director provides leadership, supervision, coaching, and strategic direction to directors and staff across these functional areas, ensuring divisional goals, constituent engagement strategies, fundraising priorities, and operational systems work together to advance the College’s mission. Primary Responsibilities 1. Strategic Leadership: Provide leadership, vision, and direction for advancement operations and engagement programs in support of the College’s mission and strategic priorities. Collaborate with the Vice President for Institutional Advancement to establish divisional goals, implement strategic initiatives, and advance a culture of philanthropy, constituent engagement, and operational excellence. 2. Leadership and Oversight of Advancement Programs: Provide strategic oversight for prospect management and research, advancement services, alumni and parent engagement, donor relations, and annual giving.  Through the supervision and development of directors and professional staff, establish priorities, monitor progress toward goals, assess outcomes, allocate resources, and ensure alignment of departmental activities with divisional and institutional objectives. 3. Staff Leadership and Development: Recruit, supervise, mentor, and develop directors and professional staff within the corresponding areas of supervision. Foster a culture of accountability, collaboration, innovation, and continuous professional growth. Empower staff leaders to assume increasing responsibility for planning, decision-making, and execution while maintaining accountability for results and organizational effectiveness. 4. Advancement Operations and Systems: Oversee advancement operations, business processes, and technology systems that support fundraising, engagement, stewardship, and reporting activities. Ensure the effective use of constituent relationship management systems, maintain high standards of data integrity and governance, and promote operational efficiencies that enhance divisional performance. 5. Campaign Planning and Execution: Partner with the Vice President and Advancement leadership to design and implement capital campaigns, fundraising initiatives, and strategic engagement efforts that support institutional priorities, academic programs, scholarships, capital projects, and student success. 6. Budget, Assessment, and Performance Management: Assist in the development and management of divisional budgets and resources. Establish measurable goals and performance indicators across advancement functions, evaluate outcomes, and implement continuous improvement strategies to enhance effectiveness and achieve organizational objectives. 7. Slate Strategy and Data Governance: Lead the ongoing optimization of Slate for Advancement and related technology solutions. Develop and improve processes that strengthen organizational effectiveness, reporting, and constituent engagement. Collaborate with campus stakeholders and external partners to ensure effective data sharing, system integration, and adherence to institutional data governance practices. 8. Institutional Collaboration: Work collaboratively with faculty, staff, college leadership, regents, and external constituents to advance fundraising and engagement priorities. Serve as a resource and partner in building relationships that strengthen the College’s philanthropic and community support. 9. Advancement Leadership: Serve as a key member of the Advancement leadership team, contributing to strategic planning, policy development, and division-wide decision-making. Promote collaboration across departments and ensure coordinated execution of Advancement priorities. 10. Other Duties: Perform other related duties as assigned in support of the Advancement Office and College mission. Supervision and Autonomy The Executive Director exercises considerable independent judgment and initiative. The position operates under general direction, referring to College policies and strategic priorities for guidance. The Executive Director supervises directors responsible for annual giving, alumni and parent engagement, advancement services, prospect management and research, and donor relations and confers with the Vice President on matters of broader institutional impact. Qualifications Education : Bachelor’s degree required; master’s degree preferred. Experience: Minimum of four years of advancement-related experience, preferably in a higher education setting. Skills: Strong leadership, management, and team-building abilities. Excellent communication and relationship-building skills. Familiarity with fundraising software (e.g., Raiser's Edge, Slate, or similar). Understanding of the mission and culture of liberal arts colleges or similar institutions. Availability: Willingness to travel and work evenings and weekends as necessary. Application Procedure Please upload the following by selecting the “Apply for this Position” below: resume a letter of interest including a statement regarding qualities within the context of the Wartburg College mission contact information for three references Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d08d19fedb018d6b803df13899&id=8a7885aca03fc28401a048b8ecc3457c": {
      "title": "Slate Captain - Institutional Advancement",
      "description": "Position: Slate Captain - Institutional Advancement Location: Waverly, IA Job Id: 614 # of Openings: 1 WARTBURG COLLEGE Title of Position: Slate Captain, Institutional Advancement Function of Position: Responsible to the Executive Director for Advancement for serving as the primary functional owner and administrator of the Advancement Customer Relationship Management (CRM) system, Technolutions Slate. The Slate Captain leads the configuration, maintenance, optimization, and governance of the Advancement CRM to support fundraising, alumni engagement, stewardship, and constituent relationship strategies. This position oversees data integrity, system workflows, reporting, integrations, and user training; collaborates with campus partners to align technology with institutional advancement goals; supervises staff and student workers as appropriate; and plans and executes CRM-related initiatives to ensure accurate, timely, and actionable data in support of institutional objectives. The incumbent works with students, colleagues, alumni, donors, and Board members, treating all with respect and maintaining the highest standards of confidentiality and data stewardship. Some evening and/or weekend work may be required. Principal Duties and Responsibilities: Serve as the primary functional administrator and subject matter expert for Slate for Advancement, overseeing system configuration, security roles, data structures, workflows, forms, portals, events, communications, automations, and reporting. Oversee the integrity, accuracy, and maintenance of the Advancement CRM and related systems, including constituent records, gift and pledge data, campaign information, prospect activity, and alumni engagement records. Lead the development, preparation, and distribution of Advancement reports, dashboards, and analytical tools to support fundraising, alumni relations, stewardship, and leadership decision-making. Manage and optimize Advancement workflows within Slate, including gift processing, online giving, stewardship communications, campaign tracking, event management, portfolio/pipeline tracking, appeal segmentation, and donor engagement activities. Serve as the primary liaison between Institutional Advancement and Information Technology Services regarding CRM integrations, data exchanges, upgrades, security, and related technology initiatives. Develop and maintain documentation, standard operating procedures, and governance; coordinate testing, annual cycle preparation, and release notes. Provide training and ongoing enablement of Advancement staff, utilizing such models as train-the-trainer, holding office hours, and championing best practices to ensure effective and consistent use of Slate. Supervise Gift Processor and Data Specialist staff and student workers as appropriate, including hiring, training, scheduling, performance development, and cross-training. Manage CRM-related projects and initiatives, including system enhancements, process improvements, testing, annual cycle preparation, and release coordination. Monitor Slate community updates and peer practices; participate in professional development and represent Institutional Advancement in campus working groups. Perform other related duties as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree required; experience administering, supporting, or as a superuser in a CRM system in a higher education, nonprofit, or advancement environment, preferred. Demonstrated understanding of advancement operations, including fundraising, gift processing, prospect research, and stewardship. Strong analytical and technical skills, including experience with database querying, reporting, and data analysis. Ability to manage multiple projects, prioritize competing demands, and meet deadlines with attention to detail and accuracy. Excellent communication, training, and collaboration skills; ability to work effectively with diverse stakeholders. Demonstrated commitment to data confidentiality, ethical data stewardship, and institutional values. Experience with Slate by Technolutions or similar CRM platforms is strongly preferred. Application Procedure: Please upload the following by selecting the “Apply for this Position” below: 1) resume 2) a letter of interest including a statement regarding qualities within the context of the Wartburg College mission 3) contact information for three references See www.wartburg.edu for further information about the college and the city of Waverly. Screening begins immediately and continues until position is filled. Wartburg College is dedicated to challenging and nurturing students for lives of leadership and service as a spirited expression of their faith and learning. Founded in 1852, Wartburg College is a selective liberal arts college internationally recognized for its community engagement and academic excellence. As indicated in the vision statement, “Wartburg College is called to be the leading institution in education of the whole person. Together, we create an inclusive community combining diverse curricular and co-curricular experiences to prepare students to be resilient leaders of positive change through service in a complex world.” Located in northeast Iowa, Waverly is an extraordinary \"gigabit\" community of more than 10,000 residents in the Cedar Valley metro near Waterloo and Cedar Falls, with an abundance of cultural, musical, and recreational opportunities. Major Midwest metropolitan areas within driving distance include Des Moines, Iowa (2.5 hours); Minneapolis/St. Paul, Minn. (3 hours); Madison, Wis. (3.5 hours); Rochester, Minn. (2 hours); Chicago (5 hours); and Omaha, Neb. (4 hours). Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d08d19fedb018d6b803df13899&id=8a7883a89e6b0bf7019e98c4f557663e": {
      "title": "Vice President for Institutional Advancement",
      "description": "Position: Vice President for Institutional Advancement Location: Waverly, IA Job Id: 601 # of Openings: 1 WARTBURG COLLEGE Title of Position – Vice President for Institutional Advancement Function of Position The Vice President for Institutional Advancement serves as the College’s chief advancement strategist and a key member of the President’s Senior Leadership Team. This role provides vision and direction for all advancement functions—including fundraising, development, constituent engagement, and alumni and parent relations—to ensure the College secures the resources, partnerships, and public visibility and support necessary to advance the mission, strategic priorities, and long-term institutional goals. In doing so, the Vice President will shape and sustain a forward-looking advancement enterprise—ensuring the technological infrastructure, analytical capabilities, and talent are aligned to enable agility, deepen engagement, and successfully support Wartburg’s evolving philanthropic priorities. Key Responsibilities Strategic Advancement Leadership Serve as the chief architect of a comprehensive advancement strategy aligned with the College’s mission, values, and strategic plan. Lead the strategic oversight of all fundraising programs, including major and planned giving, annual giving, corporate/foundation relations, stewardship, and campaign planning and execution. Develop and execute strategies that strengthen external relationships and elevate the College’s visibility, reputation, and identity within the higher-education landscape. Serve as the principal advisor to the President on advancement and fundraising initiatives, providing guidance to support presidential engagement with donors, alumni, community leaders, and other key stakeholders. Champion the modernization and integration of Wartburg’s advancement operations, including constituent relationship management (CRM) systems, data governance, and predictive analytics to identify prospective donors, optimize portfolio management, and align all advancement functions—from annual giving and alumni engagement through major and planned gifts and Board stewardship—as a coherent, institution-wide strategy for philanthropic growth. Team Leadership and Management Hire, supervise, coach, develop, and evaluate a diverse team of institutional advancement professionals. Foster a collaborative, data-informed, mission-focused, high-performing team culture that emphasizes accountability, innovation, excellence, and professional growth—while maximizing the return on the College’s finite resources. Set vision and alignment for advancement services operations including data management, prospect research, stewardship, communications workflow, and donor/alumni engagement strategies. Champion the adoption and continued development of advancement technology infrastructure to enable evidence-based decision-making, strengthen prospect identification and cultivation, and support a seamlessly connected giving pipeline from first-time donors through legacy commitments. Fundraising Excellence Lead and mentor a high-performing major gifts and planned giving team, setting clear expectations, coaching gift officers, and ensuring a disciplined approach to portfolio management and donor strategy. Develop a continuous learning model for optimizing fundraising activities that spans staff assessment and training, campaign/program design review and research, and technology enablers including artificial intelligence. Manage a personal leadership portfolio of key current and prospective donors, including members of the Board of Regents. Campus Leadership & Board Governance Shape the future of Wartburg College as a member of the President’s Senior Leadership Team, advancing institutional priorities and integrating the efforts of Institutional Advancement with other key divisions. Provide regular updates, analytics, and strategic counsel to the Senior Leadership Team and the Board of Regents regarding philanthropy, constituent engagement, and advancement progress, challenges, and opportunities. Serve as the primary liaison to the Board’s Advancement Committee, guiding volunteer leaders in their roles as advocates and ambassadors for the institution. Activate the Board of Regents as an integrated and strategically engaged node in Wartburg’s philanthropic network, cultivating Regents as informed advocates, connectors, and donors whose relationships meaningfully expand the institution’s reach among new and prospective supporters. Participate in or chair institutional committees, task forces, or working and advisory groups to strengthen institutional alignment and support shared governance. Institutional Collaboration Partner with academic and administrative leaders to ensure advancement initiatives effectively support student success, academic innovation, enrollment priorities, strategic initiatives, and institutional sustainability. Strengthen cross-campus partnerships to align advancement, enrollment, academic, and community strategies. Additional Responsibilities Lead special initiatives, strategic projects, or emerging priorities at the direction of the President. Represent the College at campus, community, and professional events to strengthen visibility and engagement. Supervision & Leadership Scope Under broad administrative direction, the Vice President sets performance standards, develops policies and procedures within advancement, and provides leadership on complex, high‑level initiatives across the College requiring institution-wide collaboration. Minimum Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in advancement, higher education administration, nonprofit management, business, communications, or a related field. Master’s degree preferred. Eight or more years of progressively responsible leadership experience and demonstrated success in fundraising. Proven track record in securing major gifts, developing donor pipelines, leading campaigns, building stakeholder relationships, and leading high‑performing teams. Experience in higher education preferred. Familiarity with data analytics, dashboard reporting, and predictive modeling as applied to prospect identification, portfolio management, or campaign strategy is strongly preferred. Application Procedure: Please upload the following by selecting the “Apply for this Position” below: 1) resume 2) a letter of interest including a statement regarding qualities within the context of the Wartburg College mission 3) contact information for three references See www.wartburg.edu for further information about the college and the city of Waverly. Screening begins immediately and continues until position is filled. Wartburg College is dedicated to challenging and nurturing students for lives of leadership and service as a spirited expression of their faith and learning. Founded in 1852, Wartburg College is a selective liberal arts college internationally recognized for its community engagement and academic excellence. As indicated in the vision statement, “Wartburg College is called to be the leading institution in education of the whole person. Together, we create an inclusive community combining diverse curricular and co-curricular experiences to prepare students to be resilient leaders of positive change through service in a complex world.” Located in northeast Iowa, Waverly is an extraordinary \"gigabit\" community of more than 10,000 residents in the Cedar Valley metro near Waterloo and Cedar Falls, with an abundance of cultural, musical, and recreational opportunities. Major Midwest metropolitan areas within driving distance include Des Moines, Iowa (2.5 hours); Minneapolis/St. Paul, Minn. (3 hours); Madison, Wis. (3.5 hours); Rochester, Minn. (2 hours); Chicago (5 hours); and Omaha, Neb. (4 hours). Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d08d19fedb018d6b803df13899&id=8a78839e9e46f651019e6615e94c17ec": {
      "title": "Dining Services Worker",
      "description": "Position: Dining Services Worker Location: Waverly, IA Job Id: 597 # of Openings: 1 WARTBURG COLLEGE Title of Position: Dining Services Worker-Part-Time If you are a Wartburg Student, please apply at Handshake. https://www.wartburg.edu/handshake/ Function of Position: Responsible to the appropriate supervisor for preparing and serving food, cleaning food service equipment and facilities, cashiering, and waiting on customers in retail dining establishments. Works in all production and greeting/cashier positions as needed, including Mensa production, Bakery production, Den, Konditorei and checking. Principal Duties and Responsibilities: Prepare food from menu, recipes and as instructed by supervisor. Operate food service equipment Cashier in retail operations and check in board operations. Label and date specified products on salad bar, deli bar, and produce coolers. Maintain, organize, and sanitize work areas. Wash dishes, pans, equipment, and all work areas. Do laundry for all dining areas. Perform other related duties as assigned. Supervision: Definite objectives are set up for the employee by the supervisor, requiring the use of a wide range of procedures. The employee plans and arranges his/her own work and refers only unusual cases to the supervisor. Minimum Qualifications: Requires basic math skills and 9 months of effective experience. Application Procedure: Please select \"Apply for this Position\" below. Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d08d19fedb018d6b803df13899&id=8a78839e9fd3ba7b01a03f7673ce2f79": {
      "title": "Career Services Coordinator",
      "description": "Position: Career Services Coordinator Location: Waverly, IA Job Id: 613 # of Openings: 1 WARTBURG COLLEGE Title of Position: Career Services Coordinator - Full-time, 12-month position Position Summary Under direction of the Director of Career Services, the Career Services Coordinator serves as the primary operational lead for employer engagement, recruitment logistics, and career events. This position expands internships, employment, and experiential learning opportunities by cultivating employer partnerships and coordinating high-impact employer-facing programs and events. The coordinator also conducts outreach to students, including individual meetings and group presentations on a variety of career readiness topics. Key Responsibilities Employer Relations Build relationships with organizations seeking Wartburg talent. Assist with recruiting and maintaining employer partnerships, with particular emphasis on alumni stakeholders. Coordinate, schedule, and participate in employer engagement visits on and off campus. Assist in developing employer partnerships that expand internship, experiential learning, and employment opportunities. Articulate the value of a Wartburg liberal arts education to key internal and external stakeholders. Career Events Coordinate career fairs and employer networking events. Manage employer registration and event logistics. Plan employer engagement initiatives, including networking receptions and industry panels, often in conjunction with Alumni Office staff. Coordinate programs such as the 40 Under 40 Career Conversations. Technology & Operations Manage employer onboarding and engagement within Handshake platform. Maintain employer records and communication within Handshake and Knight Nation. Support employer marketing and outreach efforts. Track employer engagement metrics and event participation. Collaboration & Outreach Partner with the Director of Career Services to implement employer engagement strategies. Collaborate with other members of the Career Connections Team to connect employers with student leadership initiatives and professional development programming. Support employer and student participation in job shadowing, mock interviews, and other career readiness initiatives lead by the Career Connections team. Provide career readiness programming and outreach that supports students in preparing for internships, employment, and employer engagement, including resume reviews, internship and job search strategies, and interview preparation. Support and participate in general Student Life activities and initiatives as needed and able. Qualifications Bachelor’s degree. Ability to articulate the benefits of a liberal arts education via strong writing and speaking skills. Strong attention to detail, multi-tasking, and technology skills. Excellent customer service and event planning abilities. Ability to confidently build rapport with diverse students, team members, and employers. Capable of meeting goals and deadlines in a fast-paced environment. Ability to participate in approximately four to six weeks of employer recruitment travel spaced throughout the year, including overnight and occasional weekend work. Application Procedure Please upload the following by selecting the “Apply for this Position” below: resume a letter of interest including a statement regarding qualities within the context of the Wartburg College mission contact information for three references Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d08d19fedb018d6b803df13899&id=8a78859f9e46f5eb019e65fecca90cd3": {
      "title": "Community Recreation",
      "description": "Position: Community Recreation Location: Waverly, IA Job Id: 595 # of Openings: 1 WARTBURG COLLEGE Title of Position: Community Recreation If you are a Wartburg Student, please apply at Handshake. https://www.wartburg.edu/handshake/ Community Recreation Program Assistant Function of Position: Oversee recreational programming for youth and adults as an instructor or official. Principal Job Duties and Responsibilities: Youth Sports Instructor: Review activity plan before each session. On practice days, plan specific games, drills, and skills. On game days, make sure the schedule is set. Teach fundamentals and rules of a sport. Make sure all participants learn and play the various positions of the sport. Youth Activity Instructor: Teach and supervise preschool and elementary age children during activities of arts and crafts, games, sports, and music. Be fully informed of all rules and regulations of the activity. Keep records of each day's activities. Youth Sports Official: Attend all scheduled games as assigned. Maintain control of the game by knowing the rules, make calls without hesitation, and be consistent and fair. Report game results. Adult League Supervisor: Keep records of each day's activities (i.e. attendance, game results, etc.) Duties that apply to all roles: Gather and maintain all issued equipment and materials. Dress appropriately. Arrive 15 minutes early to site to ensure environment/facility is safe. Teach concepts of good sportsmanship and ensure that it is exhibited by all participants and instructors. Promote fun and participation, not competition. Maintain good public relations with parents, staff, and spectators. Be the last person to leave the location making sure all participants have left the site, lights are off, equipment is picked up, and doors are locked. Understand policy for inclement weather and enforce it when necessary. Adhere to the policies and procedures of the Waverly Parks and Recreation Department. Assist individuals who encounter an injury and complete the proper paperwork if an incident/accident occurs. Keep the Recreation Supervisor informed of any problems (i.e. injuries, damages, etc.) that arise. Minimum Qualifications: Current CPR/AED, and First Aid Certifications Knowledgeable of sports or activity. Works well with children of all ages. Community Recreation Manager Function of Position: Oversee all activity for community rec youth flag football during evenings and weekends. Principal Duties and Responsibilities: Oversee all activity for youth flag football during evenings and weekends. Manage student employees who referee games. Schedule student employees to work certain fields for games. Communicate with teams about schedule changes. Communicate with teams about cancellations. Schedule pictures for teams. Make sure different sites have all necessary equipment. Answer questions from coaches and parents. Assist individuals who may encounter an injury and complete the proper paperwork if an incident/accident occurs. Minimum Qualifications: Current CPR/AED, and First Aid Certifications Application Procedure: Please select \"Apply for this Position\" below. Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d08d19fedb018d6b803df13899&id=8a78879e9e46f5fc019e65f42dd02213": {
      "title": "Fitness Area Attendant",
      "description": "Position: Fitness Area Attendant Location: Waverly, IA Job Id: 593 # of Openings: 1 WARTBURG COLLEGE Title of Position: Fitness Area Attendant If you are a Wartburg Student, please apply at Handshake. https://www.wartburg.edu/handshake/ Function of Position: Supervise patrons in the fitness area and maintain fitness equipment. Principal Duties and Job Responsibilities: Ensure all patrons using the fitness area are following facility policies and procedures. Maintain fitness equipment by keeping it clean and ensuring it is in its proper place. Assist individuals who encounter an injury and complete the proper paperwork if an incident/accident occurs. Minimum Qualifications: General knowledge of basic exercise guidelines and proper use of fitness area equipment. Current CPR/AED, and First Aid Certifications. Application Procedure: Please select \"Apply for this Position\" below. Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d08d19fedb018d6b803df13899&id=8a78859f9e46f5eb019e65faa9080ace": {
      "title": "Group Exercise Instructor/Personal Trainer",
      "description": "Position: Group Exercise Instructor/Personal Trainer Location: Waverly, IA Job Id: 594 # of Openings: 1 WARTBURG COLLEGE Title of Position -Group Exercise Instructor/Personal Trainer If you are a Wartburg Student please apply at Handshake. https://www.wartburg.edu/handshake/ Group Fitness Instructor Function of Position: Design, choreograph, and instruct a variety of group fitness classes in a safe and effective way for participants with various fitness levels. Principal Job Duties and Responsibilities: Design, choreograph, and instruct group fitness classes (including but not limited to high/low impact, step, pilates, yoga, kick boxing, and aqua aerobic) in a safe and effective way for participants with various fitness levels. Demonstrate proper use of equipment/props available for use with group fitness classes. Provide proper class progression throughout session. Monitor the well-being of all participants. Provide encouragement and motivation for continuation of participation. Ensure participant adherence to safety and injury prevention techniques; prepare accident reports as required. Exercises on a regular basis to maintain appropriate fitness level for instruction of classes. Maintain knowledge on fitness matters to ensure a safe class environment; participates in continuing education workshops and seminars offered. To be considered \"certified,\" individual must have a current personal training certificate from one or more of the following organizations: The Wartburg Personal Training Program offered by Wartburg College. Be sufficiently making progress towards a four-year degree in fitness. National certification from one of the following organizations: ACSM, AFAA, ACE, NSCA, NCSF, NETA, or Cooper Aerobics Institute. All other certifications will need to be cleared through the Fitness Director. A higher level of pay is given to those individuals who are certified due to the cost of certification and continuing education to maintain certification. Minimum Requirements: Fitness Equipment (Weights, Tools, Fitness related) Proficient program progression skills and proper instruction techniques required. Previous teaching experience and nutrition knowledge preferred. Current American Red Cross CPR/AED and First Aid certifications required. Group Fitness certificate preferred. Lifeguarding certification required for Aqua Group Fitness instructors. Personal Trainer Function of Position: Provide a comprehensive one-on-one educational fitness program to patrons. Principal Job Duties and Responsibilities: Evaluate fitness assessment results in order to provide an appropriate individual exercise program in congruence with goals and objectives desired by client. Design and implement individual exercise programs (in areas such as cardiovascular training, muscular endurance and strength training, flexibility, and other general fitness) for clients. Independently demonstrates and instructs clients on proper use of all cardio and weight training exercise equipment. Performs follow-up assessments to properly track client progress. Educate members on current health and fitness trends and as allowed under respective certification guidelines. Maintain complete and up-to-date client files. Maintain proper client-trainer confidentiality. Ensure client adherence to safety and injury prevention techniques; prepare accident reports as required. To be considered \"certified,\" individual must have a current personal training certificate from one or more of the following organizations: Be sufficiently making progress towards a four-year degree in fitness. National certification from one of the following organizations: ACSM, AFAA, ACE, NSCA, NCSF, NETA, IFPA, ISSA or Cooper Aerobics Institute. All other certifications will need to be cleared through the Fitness Director. A higher level of pay is given to those individuals who are certified due to the cost of certification and continuing education to maintain certification. Minimum Requirements: CSI software for tracking clientele All Fitness Related Equipment and Functional Movement Screening (FMS) Previous personal training experience and nutrition knowledge preferred. Current American Red Cross CPR/AED and First Aid certifications required. Personal Training certificate preferred. Proficient program design skills and proper spotting techniques required. Application Procedure: Please select \"Apply for this Position\" below. Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d08d19fedb018d6b803df13899&id=8a78879e9e46f5fc019e65ee028a1e6e": {
      "title": "Lifeguard/CPR Instructor",
      "description": "Position: Lifeguard/CPR Instructor Location: Waverly, IA Job Id: 592 # of Openings: 1 WARTBURG COLLEGE Title of Position - Lifeguard/CPR Instructor If you are a Wartburg Student please apply at Handshake. https://www.wartburg.edu/handshake/ Function of Position: Keep current with American Red Cross standards, teach assigned Lifeguard/CPR classes, and interpret materials provided by the American Red Cross. Principal Duties and Responsibilities: Plan, coordinate, and manage courses taught in conjunction with the local Red Cross chapter. Submit lesson plans to Aquatic Director prior to the beginning of new class sessions. Create a positive environment encouraging participants to meet course objectives. Be prepared to answer participants' questions. Knowledgeable of all personnel and operation policies, specific pool regulations, and specific emergency procedures for the pool. Administer and score the final examination when applicable. Ensure that participants meet course completion requirements. Provide positive critique and guidance to those unable to complete course requirements. Submit completed course records and reports to the Red Cross within the time required by the local Red Cross Chapter. Make three copies prior to submitting to the Red Cross for the W records. Be tactful in handling disciplinary problems and must use self-restraint in language, temper, and manners. Act and present themselves in a professional manner at all times and in all situations. Require all patrons to follow personal health and safety regulations as established by the W. Cooperate with others and complete all tasks as assigned by the shift supervisors and the Director of the W. Supervision: Assist with the maintenance of the facility and equipment including but not limited to: 1. Maintain program equipment and report all supply needs to supervisor. 2. Clean and disinfect facility area, including sauna and steam room, as directed. 3. Complete maintenance and cleaning \"rounds\" of the facility as directed. 4. Assist other personnel with their assigned duties during rush period or minor maintenance work during off periods. 5. Assist in securing the facility prior to leaving. Minimum Qualifications: Knowledge of water safety/CPR practices and usage of water safety equipment. Current Red Cross Lifeguarding Instructor training, CPR for Lay Responder, and First Aid certifications or equivalent required. Application Procedure: Please select \"Apply for this Position\" below. Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d08d19fedb018d6b803df13899&id=8a78839e9e46f651019e660664781290": {
      "title": "Welcome Desk/Climbing Wall/Child Care Attendant",
      "description": "Position: Welcome Desk/Climbing Wall/Child Care Attendant Location: Waverly, IA Job Id: 596 # of Openings: 1 WARTBURG COLLEGE Title of Position: Welcome Desk/Climbing Wall/Child Care Attendant If you are a Wartburg Student, please apply at Handshake. https://www.wartburg.edu/handshake/ Please note:  There are 3 different job descriptions listed below: Welcome Desk Function of Position: Welcome patrons of The W and assist them with any needs they may have during their visit. Principal Duties and Responsibilities: Welcome and check-in Wellness Center members. Enroll new members and modify existing memberships. Collect money for purchases and membership dues. Enroll patrons in classes at The W and for recreational programs. Check out equipment to members. Answer any questions patrons may have about the facility. Check out keys to staff members. Assist individuals who encounter an injury and complete the proper paperwork if an incident/accident occurs. Minimum Qualifications: Current CPR/AED, and First Aid Certifications Child Care Attendant Function of Position: Provide safe supervision of the W members' children that come into the childcare room. Principal Duties and Responsibilities: Provide safe supervision of the W members' children that come into the childcare room. Entertain children from ages 6 months old to 7 years old. Do AM and PM counts per sign in and sign out sheets, checking member IDs each time. Provide customer service to the W members and their children and answer questions as needed. Perform daily duties and expectations explained in the childcare manual while also adhering to the W rules. Show flexibility in assisting others with their shifts. Be responsible when opening and closing the room (i.e. MWF 8:00 am to 11 am and 4:00 pm to 7 pm) Clean the room after each shift. Minimum Qualifications: Current CPR/AED, First Aid, and Blood Borne Pathogens Certifications Knowledge of the various age groups of children (6 months to 7 years old). Proper hygiene required. Climbing Wall Attendant Function of Position: Oversee equipment and activity at the Climbing Wall. Principal Duties and Responsibilities: Pick-up key to climbing wall room and request climbing wall lights be turned on. Check out climbing wall equipment, such as harnesses, helmets, and shoes, upon a patron's presentation of a receipt. Oversee activity at the climbing wall with an emphasis on safety. Assist individuals who encounter an injury and complete the proper paperwork if an incident/accident occurs. Minimum Qualifications: Belay Certification Current CPR/AED, and First Aid Certifications To apply for any of the positions above please select \"Apply for this Position\" below: Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d08d19fedb018d6b803df13899&id=8a78879e9e46f5fc019e65ea24301cba": {
      "title": "WSI/LGI",
      "description": "Position: WSI/LGI Location: Waverly, IA Job Id: 591 # of Openings: 1 WARTBURG COLLEGE Title of Position - WSI/LGI If you are a Wartburg Student please apply at Handshake. https://www.wartburg.edu/handshake/ Function of Position: Plan, coordinate, and manage aquatic courses taught in conjunction with the local Red Cross chapter. Principal Duties and Responsibilities: Plan, coordinate, and manage courses taught in conjunction with the local Red Cross chapter. Submit lesson plans to Aquatic Director prior to the beginning of new class sessions. Create a positive environment encouraging participants to meet course objectives. Be prepared to answer participants' questions. Administer and score the final examination when applicable. Ensure that participants meet course completion requirements. Provide positive critique and guidance to those unable to complete course requirements. Submit completed course records and reports to the Red Cross within the time required by the local Red Cross Chapter. Make three copies prior to submitting to the Red Cross for the W records. Be tactful in handling disciplinary problems and must use self-restraint in language, temper, and manners. Act and present themselves in a professional manner at all times and in all situations. Require all patrons to follow personal health and safety regulations as established by the W. Knowledgeable of all personnel and operation policies, specific pool regulations, and specific emergency procedures for the pool. Cooperate with others and complete all tasks as assigned by the shift supervisors and the Director of the W. Supervision: Assist with the maintenance of the facility and equipment including but not limited to: 1. Maintain program equipment and report all supply needs to supervisor. 2. Clean and disinfect facility area, including sauna and steam room, as directed. 3. Complete maintenance and cleaning \"rounds\" of the facility as directed. 4. Assist other personnel with their assigned duties during rush period or minor maintenance work during off periods. 5. Assist in securing the facility prior to leaving. Minimum Qualifications: Knowledge of water safety practices and usage of water safety equipment. Current Red Cross Lifeguarding, CPR, and First Aid certifications or equivalent required. WSI certification preferred. Pass pre-employment tests and in-water skills test (80%), attend all in-service trainings/mandatory skill review sessions, and pass semester skill review tests (80%). Application Procedure: Please select \"Apply for this Position\" below. Apply for this Position Go back to the job list powered by"
    },
    "https://recruitingbypaycor.com/career/JobIntroduction.action?clientId=8a7883d08d19fedb018d6b803df13899&id=8a78839e9fd3ba7b01a03a9de00654f8": {
      "title": "Executive Director, Ohle Wartburg-Waverly Sports and Wellness Center",
      "description": "Position: Executive Director, Ohle Wartburg-Waverly Sports and Wellness Center Location: Waverly, IA Job Id: 612 # of Openings: 1 WARTBURG COLLEGE Title of Position – Executive Director, Ohle Wartburg-Waverly Sports and Wellness Center Function of Position The Executive Director reports to the Vice President for Strategic Recruitment and provides visionary leadership, strategic direction, and operational oversight for the Wartburg Waverly Sports and Wellness Center. This position is responsible for advancing the College’s mission through exceptional member experiences, innovative programming, community engagement, financial sustainability, and effective facility management. The Executive Director leads all aspects of Wellness Center operations, including membership services, recreation and wellness programming, fitness services, facility utilization, marketing, staff development, risk management, and revenue generation. The position serves as a key liaison between the College and the broader community while fostering a culture of wellness, service excellence, and continuous improvement. This is a full-time position and offers excellent benefits. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Strategic Leadership and Operations Provide strategic vision, planning, and leadership for all Sports and Wellness Center operations. Develop and implement initiatives that support membership growth, community engagement, campus wellness, and revenue generation. Evaluate programs and services to ensure alignment with organizational goals and community needs. Identify opportunities for innovation, expansion, and operational efficiencies. Personnel Leadership and Development Recruit, hire, train, supervise, evaluate, and support the professional development of full-time, part-time, and student staff. Foster a collaborative, customer-focused culture centered on accountability, engagement, and continuous improvement. Establish performance expectations and provide ongoing coaching and leadership development opportunities. Customer Experience and Member Engagement Develop and maintain a culture of exceptional customer service for members, guests, students, employees, and community participants. Monitor customer satisfaction and implement strategies to enhance member retention and engagement. Address operational concerns and service-related issues in a timely and effective manner. Financial Management and Revenue Growth Develop, administer, and monitor operating budgets, financial projections, membership pricing, and fee structures. Analyze financial performance and operational metrics to maximize return on investment (ROI) and support long-term sustainability. Identify and pursue new revenue-generating opportunities. Marketing and Community Relations Lead marketing, communications, and outreach efforts that promote facility programs, services, and memberships. Strengthen relationships with community organizations, businesses, and College stakeholders. Increase awareness of the Center's value and impact through strategic engagement initiatives. Facility Operations and Risk Management Ensure safe, effective, and efficient facility operations in compliance with applicable policies, regulations, and industry best practices. Oversee risk management initiatives, emergency procedures, safety protocols, and facility inspections. Maintain a welcoming, clean, and secure environment for all users. Campus and Community Collaboration Partner with the Department of Intercollegiate Athletics and other campus departments to maximize facility utilization and support institutional priorities. Collaborate with internal and external stakeholders on programming, events, and community partnerships. Technology and Systems Management Oversee operational software systems, membership management platforms, reporting tools, and related technologies. Ensure effective utilization, troubleshooting, and continuous improvement of technology systems supporting facility operations. Other Duties Perform other related duties and responsibilities as assigned. Supervision Under administrative direction, the Executive Director exercises significant independent judgment in establishing operational priorities, developing policies and procedures, managing resources, and addressing complex organizational challenges. The position is accountable for achieving strategic, financial, and operational objectives. Required Qualifications Bachelor's degree or five years of specific wellness center management/operations experience required. Three to five years of progressively responsible leadership experience. Demonstrated ability to lead teams and develop staff in a customer-focused environment. Strong communication, interpersonal, and relationship-building skills. Proven ability to collaborate effectively with diverse campus and community stakeholders. Experience with budgeting, financial management, and operational decision-making. Commitment to promoting wellness, inclusion, and exceptional customer service. Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree preferred. Experience managing operations within a health, fitness, recreation, wellness, or community center environment. Understanding of revenue generation, financial analysis, and risk management principles. Demonstrated success utilizing data and key performance indicators to improve business performance and customer satisfaction. Knowledge of membership management and recreation software platforms, including CSI software. Experience in strategic planning, marketing, and community engagement initiatives. Application Procedure: Please upload the following by selecting the “Apply for this Position” below: 1) resume 2) a letter of interest including a statement regarding qualities within the context of the Wartburg College mission 3) contact information for three references See www.wartburg.edu for further information about the college and the city of Waverly. Screening begins immediately and continues until position is filled. Wartburg College is dedicated to challenging and nurturing students for lives of leadership and service as a spirited expression of their faith and learning. Founded in 1852, Wartburg College is a selective liberal arts college internationally recognized for its community engagement and academic excellence. As indicated in the vision statement, “Wartburg College is called to be the leading institution in education of the whole person. Together, we create an inclusive community combining diverse curricular and co-curricular experiences to prepare students to be resilient leaders of positive change through service in a complex world.” Located in northeast Iowa, Waverly is an extraordinary \"gigabit\" community of more than 10,000 residents in the Cedar Valley metro near Waterloo and Cedar Falls, with an abundance of cultural, musical, and recreational opportunities. Major Midwest metropolitan areas within driving distance include Des Moines, Iowa (2.5 hours); Minneapolis/St. Paul, Minn. (3 hours); Madison, Wis. (3.5 hours); Rochester, Minn. (2 hours); Chicago (5 hours); and Omaha, Neb. (4 hours). Apply for this Position Apply with Indeed Go back to the job list powered by"
    }
  },
